// The Apps Script server: IMPLEMENTATION ONLY. The integration suite that drives it
// is a separate project, `tsconfig.test.json`, for one reason spelled out there.
//
// This project keeps EVERY strict flag inherited from the base — `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`
// above all. The code that replaces the stub (doPost.ts, DueSweep.ts, CalendarChannel.ts)
// reads rows straight out of a spreadsheet, where an unchecked index read is a live bug,
// not a test annoyance. Do not relax a flag here to make a test compile; put the test in
// the sibling project instead.
//
// `types` is set explicitly because the Apps Script globals arrive through no import:
//   google-apps-script  SpreadsheetApp, CalendarApp, ContentService, PropertiesService,
//                       LockService, Utilities, Session — the V8 runtime's globals.
//                       Types only: it emits nothing, so the shipped .gs is unchanged.
//   node                for any build-time Node surface; testkit.ts reads process.env
//                       and node:crypto/fs/path/url.
//
// `apps-script/build/` is generated output (`pnpm build:appsscript`) and is excluded. It
// is transpiled .js of what is already in src/, so checking it would mean checking
// esbuild's output rather than ours.
//
// NOTE for whoever replaces the stub: src/Code.ts is a SCRIPT, not a module. It has no
// import/export on purpose — `scripts/build-appsscript.mjs` transpiles it rather than
// bundling it, so its top-level `function doPost`/`doGet` stay globals and Apps Script
// can find them. Adding an import would turn the file into a module and break the
// deployment. Reach for the ambient `GoogleAppsScript` namespace instead.
{
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "outDir": "dist",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "types": ["google-apps-script", "node"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"],
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts", "build", "dist"]
}
